\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Changing signs at the endpoints}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{Place a sign at each endpoint of an edge. Their product is the
quantity in the sign example of \ref{fdip-00ZX}. Flipping just one
endpoint reverses that product. If the edge also carries a sign, a
flip can change the edge sign at the same time. Which three-factor
product then survives, and in which order should a group element
transport a field when the group is noncommutative?}
